missed_items.what:
UDP world-state snapshot. Acceptance: map=[owner+0x4D8] is not null-checked. If map+0x70 == 1, opcodes 7/8/9 are handled and 4 is ignored; otherwise only 4 is handled. Grammar:
bytes[4] hdr (u32 LE, copied to scene+0xEEC): timer = hdr&0x1FF, count = (hdr>>9)&0x1FF, map_id = hdr>>18
if(map_id != [map+0x1B8]) { stop }
repeat(count) { bytes[8] rec (u32 a -> scene+0xEF0, u32 b -> scene+0xEF4) }
Record bits: a[0..11] = x/2; a[12..22] = y/2; a[23] = facing (0 -> dir 2, 1 -> dir 6); a[24..29] = action (entity+0x15B4 = action+1); a[30..31] = hit flags (stored in +0x15B1; sound/effect fires on a 0 -> nonzero change); b[0] = flag (+0x15B2); b[1..25] = uid. Every record is read; a record applies to each entity with +0x98 >= 3 whose uid matches, setting target x/y at +0x15A4/+0x15A8. For 7/8/9 only (map+0x70 == 1), before the loop: scene+0xF08++; round state via FUN_00428090(scene, 0/1/2) when scene+0xF04 differs (7 -> 0, 8 -> 1, 9 -> 2). When the timer changes: 1..4 -> 'The round will start in 4..1 seconds.', 5 -> 'Fight!'; clock = [scene+0xF37]*60 - timer. The client's own sender builds this packet only on non-battle maps and sends it to 127.0.0.1.

UDP heal/restore with effects. Guard: map != null and map+0x70 == 1. Grammar:
u32 uid
if(entity(uid) == null) { stop }
bool has_hp
bool has_mp
if(has_hp != 0) { u16 hp }
if(has_mp != 0) { u16 mp }
Side effects: if has_hp, the target is the local player and the local player's HP <= 0, FUN_004307C0 runs first; hp -> +0x9C, plus local HP bar. If has_hp and not has_mp: effect/sound 0x37 at the entity. If has_mp: mp -> +0xA0, plus local MP bar and effect/sound 0x58 (the queued effect carries scene+0x220, the local uid). Effect/sound 0x54 always plays at the entity.

Version-server reply, arriving on the shared dispatcher. Grammar:
u16 version
if(version != 3 && version < 0xEA61) { stop }  (SendMessage(hDlg,0x401) starts the HTTP updater)
u16 msg_len
str[msg_len] msg (NUL is appended; set as launcher control 0x403 text; if version >= 0xEA61, also message dialog FUN_00489DA0 -> FUN_0044D4B0)
u8 server_count (owner+0x128C)
repeat(server_count) {
  u8 server_status (u32 at owner+0x1290+i*0x80)
  if(server_status != 1) {
    u8 channel_count (owner+0x130C+i*0x80)
    u8 open_count (owner+0x130D+i*0x80)
    if(open_count != 0) {
      u8 next_channel_no (1-based)
      repeat(channel_count) as j = 1.. {
        if(j == next_channel_no) {
          u16 channel_value (owner+0x129A+i*0x80+(j-1)*0xC)
          u32 channel_ip (owner+0x129C+...; host-order IPv4, htonl'd by Fireway Connect(ulong,7022))
          if(opened_so_far < open_count) { u8 next_channel_no }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
After parsing, the client closes g_sock_version. Channel slot status = 3 if present, 2 if absent. If version == 3: SetTimer(hDlg, 8, 300). ParseChannelList gets the offset BY VALUE (its own copy) and len in EDI; the PUSH EDI at 0x4404EA is the first GDP's len argument, which is why there is no POP EDI. The existing server _build_version_body matches this layout.
